2906. Construct Product Matrix
Leetcode Link: https://leetcode.com/problems/construct-product-matrix/description/?envType=daily-question&envId=2026-03-24


class Solution {
    public int[][] constructProductMatrix(int[][] grid) {
        long prod=1;
        int n=grid.length;
        int m=grid[0].length;
        int [][]ans=new int[n][m];
        for(int i=0;i<n;i++){
            for(int j=0;j<m;j++){
                prod*=grid[i][j];
            }
        }
        for(int i=0;i<n;i++){
            for(int j=0;j<m;j++){
                ans[i][j]=(int)prod/(grid[i][j]);
                ans[i][j]=ans[i][j]%12345;
            }
        }
        return ans;
    }
}

$$ The above code failed because of constraints : Overflow--total product ÷ current element.

So, following approach will prevent overflow

# Intuition:
To compute each cell’s value, we need the product of all elements except itself.
Calculating this separately for every cell would be inefficient.

Instead, we observe that the result can be formed by multiplying:

product of all elements before the current cell
product of all elements after the current cell

This avoids recomputation and eliminates the need for division.



# Approach:
Traverse the matrix from bottom-right to top-left to compute suffix products
Store the suffix product in the result matrix
Update suffix by multiplying current element (modulo applied)
Traverse from top-left to bottom-right to compute prefix products
Multiply stored suffix with prefix
Update prefix by multiplying current element (modulo applied)
Use modulo 12345 at each step to handle large values and prevent overflow
Complexity
Time complexity: O(n×m)

Space complexity: O(1)

class Solution {
    public int[][] constructProductMatrix(int[][] grid) {
        int n=grid.length;
        int m=grid[0].length;
        int [][]ans=new int[n][m];
        int mod=12345;
        long prefix=1;
        for(int i=0;i<n;i++){
            for(int j=0;j<m;j++){
                ans[i][j]=(int)prefix;
                prefix=(prefix*grid[i][j])%mod;
            }
        }
        long suffix=1;
        for(int i=n-1;i>=0;i--){
            for(int j=m-1;j>=0;j--){
                ans[i][j]=(int)((long)ans[i][j]*suffix)%mod;
                suffix=(suffix*grid[i][j])%mod;
            }
        }
        return ans;
    }
}
